    abstract:
      '<p class = "title"><strong>Experimental demonstration of Flying-Focus enhanced Thomson scattering</strong></p>\n    <div class="authors-block">\n  <p class="authors">Elias Gerstmayr<sup>1</sup>, Cristina Mariani<sup>2</sup>, Rebecca Herbst<sup>3</sup>, Matthew VanDusen-Gross<sup>4</sup>, Curtis Berger<sup>5</sup>, Qiang Chen<sup>5</sup>, Antonino Di Piazza<sup>4</sup>, Martin Stack Formanek<sup>6</sup>, Dustin Froula<sup>4</sup>, Cameron Geddes<sup>5</sup>, Anthony Gonsalves<sup>7</sup>, Ben Greenwood<sup>5</sup>, Robert Jacob<sup>5</sup>, Anthony Lu<sup>5</sup>, Aodhan McIlvenny<sup>5</sup>, Kei Nakamura<sup>5</sup>, Lieselotte Obst-Huebl<sup>5</sup>, John Palastro<sup>4</sup>, Alex Picksley<sup>5</sup>, Kristjan P\u00f5der<sup>8</sup>, Dillon Ramsey<sup>4</sup>, Hans Rinderknecht<sup>4</sup>, Gianluca Sarri<sup>1</sup>, Alexander Thomas<sup>9</sup>, Jeroen van Tilborg<sup>10</sup>, Matthew Streeter<sup>1</sup></p>\n<ol class="affiliations">\n  <li>Queen\'s University Belfast</li>\n  <li>DESY</li>\n  <li>University of Michigan</li>\n  <li>LLE</li>\n  <li>LBNL</li>\n  <li>ELI Beamlines</li>\n  <li>Lawrence Berkeley national laboratory</li>\n  <li>Deutsches Elektronen Synchtrotron DESY</li>\n  <li>university of michigan</li>\n  <li></li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n    <div class = "abstract" style = "margin-top: 10px;">\n    <p>We report the experimental demonstration of a spatiotemporally engineered \u201cchromatic Flying-Focus\u201d laser pulse to enhance x-ray generation in relativistic Thomson scattering. Precise tuning of the group delay dispersion was used to match the velocity of the focus to the trajectory of a counter-propagating laser-wakefield-accelerated electron beam. This extended the Thomson-scattering interaction, leading to an enhanced x-ray yield. This approach allows for maximising the spectral density and brightness of the x-ray beam by orders of magnitude compared to equivalent focusing without chromatic control.</p>\n    </div>\n    ',
