    abstract:
      '<p class = "title"><strong>Transverse control and optimization for plasma wakefield acceleration</strong></p>\n    <div class="authors-block">\n  <p class="authors">Yiheng Ye<sup>1</sup>, Alexander Knetsch<sup>2</sup>, Anna Kinderman<sup>3</sup>, Auralee Edelen<sup>2</sup>, Brendan O\'Shea<sup>2</sup>, CARSTEN HAST<sup>4</sup>, Carl A. Lindstr\u00f8m<sup>5</sup>, Chan Joshi<sup>6</sup>, Chaojie Zhang<sup>6</sup>, Ching-En Lin<sup>7</sup>, Claire Hansel<sup>8</sup>, Claudio Emma<sup>2</sup>, Daniel Kalvik<sup>9</sup>, Doug Storey<sup>2</sup>, Elena Ros<sup>10</sup>, Erik Adli<sup>11</sup>, Gerald Yocky<sup>7</sup>, Ivan Rajkovic<sup>2</sup>, Jinseo Park<sup>2</sup>, Juan Pablo Gonzalez-Aguilera<sup>2</sup>, Junzhi Wang<sup>2</sup>, Kelly Swanson<sup>2</sup>, Kenneth Marsh<sup>6</sup>, Marcellus Parker<sup>7</sup>, Mark Hogan<sup>2</sup>, Michael Litos<sup>8</sup>, Nathan Majernik<sup>2</sup>, Ole G. Finnerud<sup>9</sup>, Peter Kicsiny<sup>12</sup>, Ryan Loney<sup>7</sup>, Ryan Roussel<sup>2</sup>, Sebastien Corde<sup>13</sup>, Sharon Perez<sup>7</sup>, Sheldon Rego<sup>13</sup>, Spencer Gessner<sup>12</sup>, Thamine Dalichaouch<sup>6</sup>, Valentina Lee<sup>8</sup>, Viktoriia Zakharova<sup>13</sup>, Warren Mori<sup>6</sup>, Zack Buschmann<sup>7</sup></p>\n<ol class="affiliations">\n  <li>SLAC/Stanford</li>\n  <li>SLAC National Accelerator Laboratory</li>\n  <li>UCSC</li>\n  <li></li>\n  <li>DESY</li>\n  <li>University of California Los Angeles</li>\n  <li>SLAC National Accelerator Laboratory/Stanford University</li>\n  <li>University of Colorado Boulder</li>\n  <li>University of Oslo</li>\n  <li>University of Colorado at Boulder</li>\n  <li>Department of Physics, University of Oslo</li>\n  <li>SLAC</li>\n  <li>Laboratoire d\u2019Optique Appliqu\u00e9e (LOA)</li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n    <div class = "abstract" style = "margin-top: 10px;">\n    <p>Emittance preservation is one of the biggest challenges in beam-driven plasma wakefield acceleration (PWFA), demanding extremely precise control of the transverse aspect of the electron beam. We will talk about recent experimental progress in transverse control and optimization for the PWFA experiment at FACET-II in order to demonstrate a collider-quality PWFA stage. We will talk about various novel diagnostics: slice BPM dispersion measurement, beam reconstruction and optimization, etc. We will talk about the application of ML-based optimization based on beam-only measurements and plasma performance.</p>\n    </div>\n    ',
