    abstract:
      '<p class = "title"><strong>Proton Beam Focusing in Low Density Plasma from High-Repetition-Rate Liquid-Sheet Targets</strong></p>\n    <div class="authors-block">\n  <p class="authors">Jimmy Weeks<sup>1</sup>, Alexander Thomas<sup>2</sup>, Chandra Breanne Curry<sup>3</sup>, Charlotte Palmer<sup>1</sup>, Christopher Spindloe<sup>4</sup>, Claudia Parisua\u00f1a<sup>3</sup>, Cormac Hyland<sup>1</sup>, Daniel Molloy<sup>1</sup>, Daniel Symes<sup>4</sup>, Daniele Margarone<sup>5</sup>, Franziska Treffert<sup>3</sup>, George Hicks<sup>6</sup>, Griffin Glenn<sup>3</sup>, Hamad Ahmed<sup>4</sup>, James Green<sup>4</sup>, Lorenzo Giuffrida<sup>5</sup>, Martin King<sup>7</sup>, Mathew Streeter<sup>1</sup>, Maxence Gauthier<sup>3</sup>, Nicholas Dover<sup>6</sup>, Nicolas Bourgeois<sup>4</sup>, Oliver Ettlinger<sup>6</sup>, Ownen McCusker<sup>1</sup>, Paul McKenna<sup>7</sup>, Peter Parsons<sup>1</sup>, Ross Gray<sup>7</sup>, Sam Astbury<sup>4</sup>, Siegfried Glenzer<sup>3</sup>, Stephen DiIorio<sup>2</sup>, Steven Dann<sup>4</sup>, Tom Dzelzainis<sup>4</sup>, Valeriia Istokskaia<sup>5</sup>, Zulfikar Najmudin<sup>6</sup>, Brendan Loughran<sup>1</sup></p>\n<ol class="affiliations">\n  <li>Queen\'s University Belfast</li>\n  <li>Gerard Mourou Centre for Ultrafast Optical Science</li>\n  <li>SLAC National Accelerator Laboratory</li>\n  <li>Central Laser Facility</li>\n  <li>ELI Beamlines Facility, The Extreme Light Infrastructure ERIC</li>\n  <li>The John Adams Institute for Accelerator Science</li>\n  <li>Department of Physics, SUPA, University of Strathclyde</li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n    <div class = "abstract" style = "margin-top: 10px;">\n    <p>High-intensity lasers can accelerate protons from solid targets via target normal sheath acceleration (TNSA). These beams possess short pulse durations and low emittance, with potential applications in radiobiology, radioisotope production and warm dense matter. However, their inherently large divergence (10\u2019s of degrees) and the challenge of achieving multi-Hz operation need to be addressed. Building on a Gemini TA2 experiment in which proton focussing was observed in a low-density vapour from a liquid-sheet target, this presentation explores the impact of laser temporal shape, plasma profile and particle beam properties on proton beam size, presenting both simulation and experimental results.</p>\n    </div>\n    ',
