    abstract:
      '<p class = "title"><strong>Radiative damping in dielectric structures</strong></p>\n    <div class="authors-block">\n  <p class="authors">Brian Naranjo<sup>1</sup>, Atsushi Fukasawa<sup>2</sup>, Gerard Andonian<sup>3</sup>, JACKSON ROZELLS<sup>4</sup>, Jack Phillips<sup>2</sup>, James Rosenzweig<sup>2</sup>, Oliver Williams<sup>2</sup>, Pratik Manwani<sup>2</sup>, Yunbo Kang<sup>2</sup></p>\n<ol class="affiliations">\n  <li>UCLA Dept. of Physics and Astronomy</li>\n  <li>University of California, Los Angeles</li>\n  <li>UCLA</li>\n  <li></li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n    <div class = "abstract" style = "margin-top: 10px;">\n    <p>For future implementation at UCLA\'s MITHRA linac, we present a study incorporating radiative damping in dielectric wakefield accelerator (DWA) structures.  Of primary focus is manipulation of the HE11 hybrid mode, including mitigation of witness-beam break-up and production of orbital-angular momentum radiation.  Design and use of a quadrupole array for strong focusing integrated into the DWA structure is also explored.</p>\n    </div>\n    ',
